abs†info.arxiv.org .\nL156: \nL157: cite41†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite42†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL158: \nL159: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite43†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL160: cite44†About†info.arxiv.org · cite45†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite46†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite47†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L161: \nL162: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.08968] Bayesian Mixture of Experts For Large Language Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.08968)\nciteturn5911view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.08968\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Bayesian Mixture of Experts For Large Language Models\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Maryam Dialameh , cite6†Hossein Rajabzadeh , cite7†Weiwei Zhang , cite8†Walid Ahmed , cite9†Hyock Ju Kwon L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Bayesian Mixture of Experts For Large Language Models, by Maryam Dialameh and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite10†View PDF cite11†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We present Bayesian Mixture of Experts (Bayesian-MoE), a post-hoc uncertainty estimation framework for fine-tuned large language models (LLMs) based on Mixture-of-Experts architectures. Our method applies a structured Laplace approximation to the second linear layer of each expert, enabling calibrated uncertainty estimation without modifying the original training procedure or introducing new parameters.\nL17: Unlike prior approaches, which apply Bayesian inference to added adapter modules, Bayesian-MoE directly targets the expert pathways already present in MoE models, leveraging their modular design for tractable block-wise posterior estimation. We use Kronecker-factored low-rank approximations to model curvature and derive scalable estimates of predictive uncertainty and marginal likelihood.\nL18: Experiments on common-sense reasoning benchmarks with Qwen1.5-MoE and DeepSeek-MoE demonstrate that Bayesian-MoE improves both expected calibration error (ECE) and negative log-likelihood (NLL) over baselines, confirming its effectiveness for reliable downstream decision-making.\nL19: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite12†arXiv:2511.08968 [cs.LG]\nL21:    | (or cite13†arXiv:2511.08968v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL22:    | cite14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.08968†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Hossein Rajabzadeh [cite15†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 04:24:20 UTC (86 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Bayesian Mixture of Experts For Large Language Models, by Maryam Dialameh and 4 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite10†View PDF L35:   * cite11†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite16†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite17†view license L39: \nL40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.LG\nL43: \nL44: cite18†< prev |   cite19†next > L45: \nL46: cite20†new | cite21†recent | cite22†2025-11 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite23†cs L51: cite24†cs.CL L52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite25†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55: 